# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) is a variant of SKQD that replaces the need to choose an ansatz from which to sample bitstrings with an ensemble of time-evolution circuits constructed directly from the target Hamiltonian. This is achieved by subsampling smaller time-evolution operators from the Hamiltonian based on its coefficients, which is known as the qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"
msgstr "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) adalah varian SKQD yang menggantikan keharusan memilih ansatz untuk men-sampel bitstring dengan ensemble Circuit evolusi-waktu yang dibangun langsung dari Hamiltonian target. Ini dicapai dengan men-subsampel operator evolusi-waktu yang lebih kecil dari Hamiltonian berdasarkan koefisiennya, yang dikenal sebagai metode Trotterisasi qDRIFT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial makes use of [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to create the more natural fermionic circuits for the [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503) algorithm, followed by the use of fermionic layout and synthesis passes before plugging the circuits into the traditional Qiskit pipeline for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) untuk membuat Circuit fermionik yang lebih natural untuk algoritma [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503), lalu memakai pass layout dan sintesis fermionik sebelum memasukkan Circuit ke pipeline Qiskit tradisional untuk eksekusi di hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian be of the form:\n"
msgstr "Misalkan Hamiltonian berbentuk:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where, without loss of generality, we require $c_i > 0$ and that the largest eigenvalue of $h_i$ be equal, in absolute value, to $1$. Any signed or complex prefactor is absorbed into $h_i$, so the coefficients $c_i$ are strictly positive weights while the $h_i$ carry the direction of each term. Here $N$ is the number of terms (or, after grouping, the number of groups) in the Hamiltonian; it is a property of the Hamiltonian and is distinct from the number of operators sampled into a single circuit, written $n$ below.\n"
msgstr "di mana, tanpa mengurangi keumuman, kita mensyaratkan $c_i > 0$ dan eigenvalue terbesar dari $h_i$ sama, dalam nilai absolut, dengan $1$. Prafaktor bertanda atau kompleks apa pun diserap ke dalam $h_i$, sehingga koefisien $c_i$ adalah bobot yang benar-benar positif sementara $h_i$ membawa arah tiap suku. Di sini $N$ adalah jumlah suku (atau, setelah pengelompokan, jumlah kelompok) dalam Hamiltonian; ia adalah properti Hamiltonian dan berbeda dari jumlah operator yang disampel ke dalam satu Circuit, ditulis $n$ di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT algorithm then realizes, for the target time $t$, some operator $V_k$, where $k$ goes from $1 \\cdots K$ and signifies the $k_{th}$ SqDRIFT circuit, defined as:\n"
msgstr "Algoritma qDRIFT kemudian merealisasikan, untuk waktu target $t$, suatu operator $V_k$, di mana $k$ berjalan dari $1 \\cdots K$ dan menandakan Circuit SqDRIFT ke-$k_{th}$, didefinisikan sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $n$ is the number of sampled operators per circuit and $K$ is the number of circuits in the ensemble. The product runs over the $n$ draws, not over all $N$ Hamiltonian terms, and because the terms are drawn with replacement, the same $h_i$ can appear more than once in a single $V_k$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini $n$ adalah jumlah operator yang disampel per Circuit dan $K$ adalah jumlah Circuit dalam ensemble. Perkaliannya berjalan atas $n$ pengundian, bukan atas semua $N$ suku Hamiltonian, dan karena suku diundi dengan pengembalian, $h_i$ yang sama bisa muncul lebih dari sekali dalam satu $V_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity:\n"
msgstr "Besaran:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is the $L_1$ norm of the coefficients, so each of the $n$ steps evolves for the same duration $\\lambda t / n$ regardless of which term was drawn. The uniformity of the step angle is the characteristic feature of qDRIFT: a coefficient influences the result through *how often* its term is drawn, not through how far that term is rotated. The indices are sampled from the distribution:\n"
msgstr "adalah norma $L_1$ dari koefisien, sehingga masing-masing dari $n$ langkah berevolusi selama durasi yang sama $\\lambda t / n$ terlepas dari suku mana yang diundi. Keseragaman sudut langkah adalah ciri khas qDRIFT: sebuah koefisien memengaruhi hasil lewat *seberapa sering* sukunya diundi, bukan lewat seberapa jauh suku itu dirotasi. Indeks-indeksnya disampel dari distribusi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the series $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ is a random sequence of term indices drawn from this distribution. Since the $c_i$ are positive and sum to $\\lambda$, this is a normalized probability distribution, and the expectation of the resulting channel over the random draws approximates evolution under $H$, with an error that decreases as $n$ grows. Note that the approximation error depends on $\\lambda$ rather than on the number of terms $N$.\n"
msgstr "jadi deret $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ adalah urutan acak indeks suku yang diundi dari distribusi ini. Karena $c_i$ positif dan berjumlah $\\lambda$, ini adalah distribusi probabilitas ternormalisasi, dan ekspektasi kanal yang dihasilkan atas undian acak mendekati evolusi di bawah $H$, dengan galat yang menurun seiring $n$ bertambah. Perhatikan bahwa galat aproksimasi bergantung pada $\\lambda$, bukan pada jumlah suku $N$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The SqDRIFT paper writes the number of terms as $\\mathcal{N}$ and the sequence length as $N$; we use $N$ and $n$ here to keep the two clearly distinct.)\n"
msgstr "(Paper SqDRIFT menulis jumlah suku sebagai $\\mathcal{N}$ dan panjang urutan sebagai $N$; kita memakai $N$ dan $n$ di sini agar keduanya tetap jelas berbeda.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to generate an ensemble of such randomized circuits. After we have created these circuits, similar to how we create a Krylov subspace for different operators, we sample bitstrings from multiple such operators with different time parameters. This ensures a higher overlap between the ground state vectors and sampled bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara membuat ensemble Circuit acak seperti itu. Setelah Circuit-Circuit ini dibuat, mirip cara kita membuat subruang Krylov untuk operator yang berbeda, kita men-sampel bitstring dari beberapa operator seperti itu dengan parameter waktu yang berbeda. Ini memastikan overlap yang lebih tinggi antara vektor keadaan dasar dan bitstring yang disampel.\n"

